---
source: crates/holst-cli/src/table.rs
expression: "help_of(&format!(\"{line} -h\"))"
---
Unlock what `o lock` locked: a locked group is dissolved and its objects stay, a locked frame or table is unlocked. The objects are the linked object and every --object; --all unlocks everything locked on the board.
Needs the board's right to manage locks. It prints one line per changed object with @N and its link.

USAGE
  holst object unlock <board> [flags]

ARGUMENTS
  board   The board: id, link or part of its name

FLAGS
      --object object   A locked group, frame or table, repeat for several: id, link, @N or the first 8 characters of its id
      --all             Unlock everything locked on the board
  -w, --workspace ws    Where names are looked up and new things go: a workspace id or part of its name; all of yours by default
  -n, --dry-run         Show what would change; change nothing

INHERITED FLAGS
  --output, --verbose, --base-url, --home, --no-cache, --help   as in `holst -h`

EXAMPLES
  $ holst o unlock "Roadmap" --object a1b2c3d4
  $ holst o unlock "Roadmap" --all -n

LEARN MORE
  How a board is given: `holst b -h`.
  Exit codes: `holst help exit-codes`.
